   191	
   192	```bash
   193	python3 scripts/harden.py results/2003.14361/gen_2003_14361.py
   194	bash scripts/emit.sh 2003.14361 20 hard
   195	```
   196	
   197	## Caveats
   198	
   199	This is a narrow promise subclass, not unrestricted correspondence colouring:
   200	the cover is 2-fold, satisfiable, bipartite, regular, and admits affine rules on
   201	public Boolean codes. A tool-enabled solver should use the anchor formula or
   202	signed BFS and will solve it quickly; that is the Track B premise. The
   203	0/200,000 number samples uniform correctly shaped affine rules and says nothing
   204	about a solver that has found the coboundary invariant. The protected-anchor
   205	switch chain is not a proof of uniform sampling from regular bipartite graphs.
   206	No SAT, ILP, or spectral implementation was benchmarked because exact signed
   207	propagation strictly dominates them on this 2-fold subclass. The canonical key
   208	uses distance spectra, the strongest cheap invariant implemented here; such
   209	spectra can theoretically collide for nonisomorphic coded covers even though
   210	all 20 unrelated audit seeds were distinct. Most importantly, the required
   211	multi-vendor no-tool evidence is absent until the external quota block clears.

