codex
Implemented and locally verified a native Track B generator based on the paper’s correspondence-cover definition (§2.1), while respecting its algorithmic caveat (§8.4). [Paper full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2003.14361).

Key results:

- Inverse-generated affine 2-fold correspondence colourings.
- Exactly 2 valid answers among `2^34`; 0/200,000 random guesses succeeded.
- Five attacks failed 0/8.
- Reference XOR/BFS algorithm succeeds 8/8: 39,200 operations, 0.023909 s mean.
- Canonicalization passed 140/140 affine/relabeling tests.
- Answer: 88 characters, 34 atoms; intended shortcut: 33 XORs.
- Deterministically connected instances via a retained shuffled spanning cycle.

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/gen_2003_14361.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Status remains **parked, not shippable**: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every redraw. Those records are provider errors, not model failures, so the required multi-vendor hardness claim cannot honestly be made until quota is restored. No `REJECTED.md` was created because G, V, and all local gates pass; only external STEP 4 evidence is unavailable.
