-signed BFS and will solve it quickly; that is the Track B premise. The
-0/200,000 number samples uniform correctly shaped affine rules and says nothing
-about a solver that has found the coboundary invariant. The protected-anchor
-switch chain is not a proof of uniform sampling from regular bipartite graphs;
-the retained shuffled Hamilton cycle guarantees connectivity but also makes the
-base-graph distribution nonuniform. No SAT, ILP, or spectral implementation was
-benchmarked because exact signed propagation strictly dominates them on this
-2-fold subclass. The canonical key uses affine difference multiplicities plus
-deterministic graph colour refinement. It is invariant under the audited affine
-relabellings but can theoretically collide for nonisomorphic coded covers, even
