codex
Built and locally verified, but parked rather than falsely shipped.

The Track B generator uses the paper’s native correspondence-cover objects from Section 2.1 and reflects its algorithmic caveats in Section 8.4. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.14361)

Key results:

- Exactly 2 valid polynomial witnesses among \(2^{92}\).
- 0/200,000 structured random guesses.
- Six adversarial attacks each failed 0/8.
- Reference signed-BFS solved 8/8 in 61,866 operations.
- Answer: 204 characters, 92 atoms.
- Compact route: 235 XOR operations.
- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/gen_2003_14361.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.14361/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The remaining blocker is external: all twelve oracle calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” leaving zero scored attempts. Consequently no hardness verdict is claimed and the module was not emitted or submitted.
